ORIGINAL AUTHOR AND METHOD

The original Photo Material Intervention workflow and its first three recipes
(Portal Woodcut, Paint-Stop Charcoal, and Sunlight Screenprint) were authored
and first publicly released by Pilipala9919 in 2026.

The method's identifying sequence is:

1. diagnose the photographic subject, strongest structure, anchors, and fidelity risks;
2. choose one subject-appropriate handmade or print medium by mark affinity rather than by a preset style;
3. derive a visible transition boundary from source geometry, light, weather, motion, depth, or contact;
4. preserve truthful photographic anchors and separate genuine obstruction removal when needed;
5. use a strict default budget of one diagnosis, one medium decision, one generation, and at most one local repair.

